(Smoke test lecture: The Water Cycle) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Evaporation: the sun heats water in oceans, lakes and rivers and turns it into water vapour.) Tj T*
(Transpiration: plants release water vapour from their leaves into the air.) Tj T*
(Condensation: as vapour rises it cools and forms tiny droplets, which make clouds.) Tj T*
(Precipitation: when droplets combine and grow heavy they fall as rain, snow, sleet or hail.) Tj T*
(Collection: water gathers in oceans, lakes, rivers and underground aquifers.) Tj T*
(Infiltration: some water soaks into the soil and becomes groundwater.) Tj T*
(Runoff: water that does not soak in flows over land into streams and rivers.) Tj T*
(The cycle is driven by energy from the sun and by gravity, and it has no start or end.) Tj T*
ET
